{
  "dom_id": "step-q346101",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The following table shows the fuel consumption rate, $F(t),$ of a generator (in liters per hour) over a period of $8$ hours.\n\n| $t\\,\\text{(hours)}$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F\\,\\text{(liters/hour)}$ | $4$ | $3$ | $5$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nUse the right Riemann sum for $F(t)$ over the interval $[0,8]$ with four subintervals to approximate the total amount of fuel used.\n\nThe total amount of fuel is \n{{field-1}} liters.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's compute the step size $Δt,$ which is just the width of each rectangle. In this case, the endpoints of our interval are $a=0$ and $b=8,$ and there are $n=4$ rectangles, so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔt=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{8-0}{4}=2.\n$$\n\nThe area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{F(2)+F(4)+F(6)+F(8)}})\\cdot {{Δt}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $F(t)$ at each point:\n\n| $t$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(t)$ | $3$ | $5$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(3+5+2+6)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total amount of fuel used over a period of $8$ hours. So, the total amount of fuel is $32$ liters.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
